# MaCSad administrative header

The header identifies the research workspace without owning application state.

## Component AdminHeader
View:
    <header class="topbar">
      <div class="brand"><div class="brand-mark">M∴</div>
        <div class="brand-copy"><strong>MaCSad</strong><span>Math + computer science auto-discovery</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="top-status"><span class="pulse"></span><span>Research workspace preview</span></div>
    </header>
Style:
    .topbar { min-height: 74px; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 24px;
      padding: 16px clamp(20px,4vw,56px); color: #f8f6ef; background: #102c3b; border-bottom: 1px solid #445963; }
    .brand { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 14px; }
    .brand-mark { width: 38px; height: 38px; display: grid; place-items: center; border-radius: 12px; color: #102c3b; background: #d8ff72; font: 800 14px/1 ui-monospace, monospace; }
    .brand-copy strong { display: block; font-size: 16px; letter-spacing: .02em; }
    .brand-copy span { display: block; margin-top: 2px; color: #b8cad1; font-size: 12px; }
    .top-status { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; color: #c9d7dc; font-size: 12px; }
    .pulse { width: 8px; height: 8px; border-radius: 999px; background: #d8ff72; }
    @media (max-width: 820px) { .top-status { display: none; } }
